{"t": 35.622, "n": 29, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I wrote the triage note to `plugins/tempergraph/docs/tasks/i21b.triage.md`. I used that folder because the specs live under the plugin's `docs/`. I didn't run git, so the engine has to commit it.\n\n- **Rule files:** I opened `task-notes.rule.md` and `documents.rule.md` with the read tool.\n- **Acceptance criteria:** I copied the task's six criteria into the note as written.\n- **Gaps:** There are four, and none is covered by an existing spec. All four are findable, so the Owner decisions section says `None`.\n  - **G1 (spec update, `executor-claude-code`, ECC-B13 and ECC-B19):** A step that declares an MCP server the operator's configuration doesn't define is launched silently without it. The spec doesn't say it must be refused or recorded.\n  - **G2 (spec update, `executor-claude-code`, ECC-B13 and ECC-B18):** A CLI whose help doesn't list `--strict-mcp-config` isn't refused at preflight. The flag is sent unconditionally.\n  - **G3 (existing behaviour, `lifecycle-and-evals` LIF-B7 to LIF-B16):** No spec says the confirmed version in `executor_compat.json` must be in its `recorded` list. The file names 2.1.332 as confirmed but records only 2.1.329.\n  - **G4 (spec update, `executor-claude-code`, ECC-B13):** The spec doesn't say the P-CC-13 probe reads a turn after the servers have connected. The current test reads only `system/init`.\n- **Route:** Deliver is `code` and the route is `discovery`, not `quick`, because gaps exist.\n\nARTIFACT triage_note: plugins/tempergraph/docs/tasks/i21b.triage.md\nARTIFACT gaps: some\nARTIFACT route: discovery\nARTIFACT covered: no", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "607c7847-3cea-4782-8dcb-b531c7c70522"}
